# Bulk ORACC downloads: 30 MB of zips + 42 MB of scraped HTML, both exactly
# reproducible from scripts/fetch_babylonian.py and
# scripts/fetch_babylonian_translations.py. The extracted snapshot that the
# annotation actually rests on, data/raw/babylonian/translations.jsonl, IS
# tracked, so the "store raw first" rule still holds for anything we reason
# from -- we just don't version 72 MB that a script regenerates.
data/raw/babylonian/oracc_json/
data/raw/babylonian/oracc_html/
